Roast.pet Frontier Stack =E2=80=94 1 useful find remove.bg API migration to
Leonardo.Ai =E2=80=94 ADOPT NOW as a dependency-risk decision

Source: https://www.remove.bg/api
Verified: 2026-09-19. remove.bg=E2=80=99s official API page now states that
starting December 1, 2026, background removal moves to Leonardo.Ai (also
part of Canva). Existing remove.bg PAYG credits expire December 1, 2026 at
09:00 CET. Source pricing page: https://www.remove.bg/pricing

WHAT CHANGED
This is not a new segmentation model; it is a material infrastructure
change for one of the most common production background-removal APIs.
remove.bg is directing API users to Leonardo.Ai. The migration pitch adds
upscaling, generated scenes, still-to-video and multi-step Blueprint
chaining around background removal.

ROAST.PET RELEVANCE
Do not build Roast.pet=E2=80=99s PetPrep contract around remove.bg now. Our
existing local-first direction becomes more valuable: local/browser
segmentation for normal uploads, a provider-neutral fallback for hard fur,
and no dependency on a service entering migration.

INPUT / OUTPUT
Current remove.bg: animal/product image upload or URL -> transparent image
/ alpha matte / JPG/WebP/PNG. Leonardo migration is positioned as
background removal plus upscale, generated scenes and video in chained
Blueprints.

API / INSTALL ROUTE
Current remove.bg remains a simple HTTP API until the migration date. For
Roast.pet, retain PetPrep as an internal interface and implement local
BiRefNet/Alphaveil plus Knockout fallback rather than adding a new remove.b=
g
dependency. Leonardo can later be benchmarked behind the same interface.

PRICING
remove.bg currently shows $3 for 3 PAYG credits and $9/month for 40
credits; credits expire Dec 1, 2026. Local processing remains effectively
$0 marginal inference on the customer device; the previously identified
Knockout fallback is about $0.02/image.

COMMERCIAL LICENSE
remove.bg is a commercial API. Leonardo terms should be separately checked
before production migration; do not infer identical rights merely because
Canva owns both.

PRIVACY / SELF-HOSTING
remove.bg is cloud processing; its privacy page says API images are deleted
immediately after processing. Local Roast.pet preprocessing remains
preferable because raw customer pet photos need not leave the browser.
Leonardo is likewise a hosted route rather than a self-hosting answer.

QUALITY / LATENCY
No evidence this hour establishes that Leonardo background removal is
better on difficult pet fur than our local/fallback candidates. Treat the
migration as a dependency event, not a quality upgrade.

EXACT ROAST.PET USE CASE
Customer uploads dog/cat photo -> browser/local cutout -> automatic
edge/fur QC -> Knockout or other fallback only when QC fails -> canonical
transparent PetAsset. Do not add remove.bg as an intermediate dependency.

SMALLEST TEST
Build a 50-image hard-pet corpus (white-on-white fur, black-on-dark fur,
long hair, motion blur, multiple animals, clutter). Freeze it as the
PetPrep regression suite. Score local BiRefNet/Alphaveil, Knockout and
Leonardo when its migration endpoint is production-ready. Metrics: fur
recall, halo pixels, missing ears/tails/whiskers, latency, cost and
upload/privacy requirement.

DECISION: ADOPT NOW =E2=80=94 not the service, the abstraction and migratio=
n
avoidance.

TOP 5 STACK CHANGES TO TEST NOW

   1. Freeze a hard-pet PetPrep benchmark and local -> QC -> hosted
   fallback contract.
   2. P-Video-2-Pro Speed for cheap best-of-N draft generation.
   3. LongCat vs H3 Max vs Wan 2.7 specifically on cats/dogs.
   4. Multi-take TTS -> comedy ranking before paying for animation.
   5. Audiovisual QC -> automatic retry / premium-render escalation.

CHEAPEST MEANINGFUL CAPABILITY IMPROVEMENT
Local browser segmentation remains effectively $0 marginal inference and
now also reduces migration/vendor risk.

BIGGEST CAPABILITY SHOCK THIS HOUR
No genuinely new image/video foundation-model release cleared the
threshold. The useful change is operational: remove.bg has an explicit Dec
1 migration deadline, so a new Roast.pet implementation should avoid
coupling to it.

CONCRETE STACK REPLACEMENT / SIMPLIFICATION
Standardize one PetPrep contract:
LOCAL -> EDGE/FUR QC -> HOSTED FALLBACK -> canonical transparent PetAsset

Keep remove.bg/Leonardo/Knockout interchangeable behind the fallback
boundary. This prevents a vendor migration from touching Etsy intake, card
generation, video, AR or POD stages.

SCAN NOTES
Fresh searches covered GitHub/Hugging Face/arXiv-style release queries,
fal/Replicate surfaces, lip-sync/avatar, segmentation, WebXR/AR,
Shopify/Etsy/POD and workflow tooling. H3 Max, LongCat, P-Video-2-Pro,
ModelRunner and other findings from previous runs were suppressed rather
than repeated. No padding with unchanged mature tools.

